  "doc": {
    "description": "15 -- ALU: a parameterized arithmetic-logic unit (capstone).\n\nCombines most of the language in one design: imports, a parameter\npassed down the hierarchy, generators for the bitwise lanes, a\nconstant for the adder carry-in, a 4-way mux on the result, `when`\nboundary folding, and an OR-reduction for the Zero flag.\n\n    Op = 0b00  ->  R = A AND B\n    Op = 0b01  ->  R = A OR  B\n    Op = 0b10  ->  R = A XOR B\n    Op = 0b11  ->  R = A +   B\n\nCout is the adder's carry and is meaningful only when Op = 0b11.\nRequires N >= 2 (the Zero-flag reduction chain).",
    "source": "circuit.shdl",
